  CardStory: "Twain looks in the mirror. \r\n \r\nIt\u2019s new and cheap, like all
    the other ones which have been installed in regular intervals across the barracks.They
    are nothing special. Serviceable.\r\n\r\nHe gives himself a good look. His uniform
    is not impeccable, but it is still within regulations. black eyes with bags under
    them, the consequence of one too many late nights on the training courts. \r\n\r\nMost
    of all, he feels the weight of the spikes that adorn his shoulders, marking his
    division and rank. Adorn\u2026 Is not the right word. These are part of him,
    now, jutting out from his bones, feeding on his marrow, making him stronger,
    faster. Making him more.\r\n\r\nAnd he will need to be more, if he is to keep
    up with the rest.\r\n\r\nTwain moves his hand up to adjust his lapel and his
    reflection follows, after which he passes a thin comb through black locks and
    tames the worst of his bed hair.\r\n\r\nServiceable, for a first day. He hopes
    it will be enough."
